  "selection": {
    "rule": "TOS, the relative selection metric of Shaha et al., IEEE RAAICON 2021",
    "formula": "TOS_i = 0.5 * (tanh(z_acc_i) - tanh(z_err_i)), z-scores taken across the candidate pool with the population standard deviation",
    "why": "Every candidate above the baseline lies within roughly one standard deviation of every other on accuracy, so a single headline number cannot separate them, and picking the largest one silently treats a missed landslide and a false alarm as equally expensive. TOS requires both axes to be named.",
